I see similar behavior for arguments to decorators.  Perhaps just another manifestation of the same underlying bug?

```
def dec(x):
  def d(func):
    return func
  return d

class C(object):
  X = [1, 2]
  Y = (x for x in X)  # pylint doesn't complain

  @dec([x for x in X])  # pylint complains
  def f(self):
    pass
```
